{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.DegreeTwoBaryonWeight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.DegreeTwoBaryonWeight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BaryonWeight.beta2_approx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BaryonWeight.beta2_approx","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/degree-two-baryon-weight.lean#L37-L42","doc":"At q₀: β₂ ≈ -6.087. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:degree-two-baryon-weight","label":"prop:degree-two-baryon-weight","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/degree-two-baryon-weight.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BaryonWeight.beta2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BaryonWeight.beta2","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/degree-two-baryon-weight.lean#L31-L35","doc":"β₂ = -2[3]_q arises from the baryon quantum number:\n3 color channels produce C(3,2) = 3 pairwise products,\nq-deformed to [3]_q. Factor -2 from pn doubling and\nalternating channel sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BaryonWeight.qInt3_approx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BaryonWeight.qInt3_approx","kind":"theorem","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/degree-two-baryon-weight.lean#L24-L29","doc":"At q₀ = 1.10998: [3]_q ≈ 3.044. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BaryonWeight.qInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BaryonWeight.qInt","kind":"def","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/degree-two-baryon-weight.lean#L17-L22","doc":"Quantum n-integer [n]_q = (q^n - q^{-n}) / (q - q^{-1}). ","signatureChunk":0}]}